# Toy control (D-210, PR-15, F-4, F-72, R5; an audio toy of plan 05-07): the noise LFSR feedback without tap 12 (taps 0, 1, 11, 17 instead of 0, 1, 11, 12, 17; D-193, ASSUMED LED-AUD-0010), made from the live src/core/psg.c by scripts/control-mutate. The anchor is the one
# tap expression of lfsr_step; the replacement drops the term s >> 12. The case audio_mod_noise4 must come out guest_failure: its noise_seq group n4_seq reads another sequence from ordinal 7 on (the window holds ordinals 8 to 118), while its seed-free groups two_level, run_grid
# and run_min stay green (two levels on the grid of 14 samples whatever the sequence). The cases with the second column pass must STAY pass (F-4): audio_mod_noise5 judges no sequence (two_level, run_grid and noise_ratio only: the seed-free proof) and audio_tone_sel0 plays no noise.
tag=rule-psg-noise-taps
file=src/core/psg.c
anchor=uint32_t b = (s ^ (s >> 1) ^ (s >> 11) ^ (s >> 12) ^ (s >> 17)) & 1u;
